{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Waters of ḥaṭaʾt.</b> Like תחטאני, or its meaning is like the sin-offering of the sacrifice." "<b>Sprinkle upon them.</b> Rabbi Moses said that the hafel has a nun as its first letter, like הכה תכה, and it is correct." "<b>And let a razor pass over all their flesh.</b> Now they had already passed a razor — the transmitters said: even the beard, but not the forelock [pe'ah]." "<b>And wash their garments.</b> And afterward they shall be pure, when they are purified with the waters of ḥaṭaʾt." "<b>And they shall be purified.</b> From the hitpa'el [reflexive/passive] binyan, and the tav is absorbed [muvla'at]. And likewise המקדשים and המטהרים."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:48.981175965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}